I’m a midwife, not a keeper of flocks, so ye’d best ask the right person hereabouts if ’tis a fox, a stray hound, or something worse. I only know how to ease a ewe in labour or steep a willow-bark draught for a fever, and I’ve no skill for reading tracks in the mud. I hope the flock is safe enough, but I must be off to tend a young mother down the lane. Slán leat.
