Well, Father Cathal has his books and his rosary, but when a woman’s labour turns hard or a babe won’t take the breast, it’s the willow-bark tea and the steady hands that see her through, not a sermon from the pulpit. I’ll keep my herbs in the jar and my prayers in my heart, and let him tend to souls while I mind the mothers. Le cúnamh Dé, we’ll both be doing the Lord’s work in our own fashion.
